      "content": "USB 3.1 allows the use of receiver equalization to meet system timing and voltage margins. For long cables and channels the eye at the Rx is closed, and there is no meaningful eye without first applying an equalization function. The Rx equalizer may be required to adapt to different channel losses using the Rx EQ training period. The exact Rx equalizer and training method is implementation specific.",
